   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Christ's College, St Andrew's Street front south of the Great Gate (p0 = gate end, p1 = SE corner). Ashlar range of two storeys under a battlemented parapet (parapet from the cornice line ~7.9 m to the eaves). Projecting string course over the ground floor. About 13 regular bays ~2.85 m apart from the SE corner: ground floor two-light stone-mullioned windows with Tudor-arched lights, first floor taller two-light windows; a small corbelled oriel at first floor near mid-length by a downpipe. No street door on this stretch. Bay count read from an oblique view (mapillary 4171158462949779) and checked against 948123169335639; spacing approximate."
  },
