   "notes": "Christ's College, south gable end of the St Andrew's Street range (p0 = corner with the battlemented street front). Ashlar, two storeys under a coped gable with a chimney: ground-floor three-light stone-mullioned window, moulded string course, and a four-light corbelled oriel at first floor, both slightly left of centre. Read from mapillary 316741473376513 (frontal from the south) and 916179375900871, 485497869555323. Refined with Geograph 767310 (Christ's Lane, frontal): five-light ground window and five-light corbelled oriel, both ~x 4.2; small battlemented turret at the p1 corner (not modelled)."
